import TpuSyncVerify.Common.ListAux
import TpuSyncVerify.Transfer.Session

/-!
# Bounded host layer staging manager (`StagingLayerManager`)

Shared per-session slot manager `tpu_raiden::StagingLayerManager`
(`tpu_sync/kv_cache/staging_manager.{h,cc}`), together with the host-layer
count resolution helpers (`ResolveEnvNumStagingLayers` and
`CheckAllLayersHaveHostBuffers` in `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_base.cc`).

When fewer host layer buffers are allocated than device layers (or pools), a
transfer session multiplexes its `num_layers` logical units over `num_slots`
physical host layer buffers `[0, num_slots)`. `staging.{h,cc}` are
`tpu_sync/kv_cache/staging_manager.{h,cc}`; `base.h`/`base.cc` are
`tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_base.{h,cc}`.

## State, operations, and lock scopes

| Field / operation | C++ | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `numSlots` | `num_slots` passed to `StagingLayerManager(size_t)` | physical host layer buffers `[0, numSlots)` |
| `free` | `free_` (`std::deque<size_t>`) | FIFO queue of unleased slots (`head` = `front()`, `++ [s]` = `push_back(s)`) |
| `leases` | `leases_` (`absl::flat_hash_map<size_t, size_t>`) | active `(unit, slot)` pairs |
| `shutdown` | `shutdown_` (`bool`) | set by `Shutdown()`; wakes and cancels `Acquire` |
| `acquire` | `StagingLayerManager::Acquire` | return existing lease, pop head of `free`, block (`none`), time out, or cancel |
| `lookup` | `StagingLayerManager::Lookup` | query `unit`'s active slot lease |
| `release` | `StagingLayerManager::Release` | erase `unit`'s lease and append its slot to the tail of `free` |
| `releaseAll` | `StagingLayerManager::ReleaseAll` | return every leased slot to `free` and clear `leases` |
| `doShutdown` | `StagingLayerManager::Shutdown` | set `shutdown := true` |
| `numFree` | `StagingLayerManager::num_free` | `free_.size()` |

Every field (`free_`, `leases_`, `shutdown_`) is `ABSL_GUARDED_BY(mu_)`.
`Lookup`, `Release`, `ReleaseAll`, `Shutdown` and `num_free` each execute under
a single `absl::MutexLock lock(mu_)`. `Acquire` holds `mu_` across its initial
check, sleeps inside `mu_.AwaitWithDeadline(absl::Condition(&ready), ...)`
(atomically releasing and re-acquiring `mu_`), and mutates `free_` / `leases_`
before unlocking `mu_`; a caller still blocked inside `AwaitWithDeadline`
(`acquire = none`) has not yet mutated `StagingLayerManager` state.

## Properties

Proved for every `StagingLayerManager` satisfying `Inv` (`inv_init`,
`acquire_inv`, `release_inv`, `releaseAll_inv`, `doShutdown_inv`):
* **Slot conservation (`Inv.conservation`)**: `free.length + leases.length = numSlots`.
* **Slot exclusivity (`lookup_injective`, `lookup_not_mem_free`)**: distinct
  units never lease the same slot, and no leased slot appears in `free`.
* **Host buffer bounds (`lookup_lt`)**: every leased slot is `< numSlots`.
* **Idempotent re-acquisition (`acquire_idempotent`)**: an already-leased unit
  gets `some (.leased slot m)` without waiting even when `free` is empty.
* **Cleanup & cancellation (`release_noop_of_none`, `releaseAll_numFree`,
  `shutdown_cancels`)**: releasing an unleased unit is a no-op, `releaseAll`
  restores `numFree = numSlots`, and `shutdown = true` cancels `acquire` when
  `0 < numSlots`.

